                "kind": "law",
                "authority": "Obsmetrologia",
                "revision": "Closure/Regime.lean",
                "locator": "Closure/Regime.lean (strict kappa < omega, Scott kappa = omega, transfinite-bounded omega < kappa < omega_1, aperiodic kappa >= omega_1)",
                "applicability": "Applies to every EavtCellAnswer's proof-kind tag.",
                "statement": "The answer passes through stratify's closure and regime exactly; a finite trace's fold always reaches its fixed point in finitely many passes, so regime is always \"strict\" here and the operation never invents an aperiodic classification.",
                "sourceSpan": {
                    "type": "ArtifactFabricationSourceSpan",
